    description: "Repro: `locals { name = var.region }` -> no edge; `lower(var.region)` -> same edge id twice (deduped later by cli.py ~12551, so only direct callers see it); `source = \"../net\"` -> no imports edge while `./a` gets one.\n\nFound by the 2026-10-10 docstring-staleness audit (reviewer + default-REJECT verifier, reproduced). Notebook: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_10102026.md."  # 88a3
    fields:  # 88a3
      statement: "Every resolvable HCL reference produces one depends_on edge from its enclosing block, and every local module source produces an imports edge."  # 88a3
      root_cause: "_find_enclosing_block_symbol (hcl.py ~342-349) handles only resource/data/module/output; each nested expression node is walked over its whole subtree; module imports require startswith('./')."  # 88a3
